  "conclusion": "Both estimators share the channels, the seeds and the stopping rule. The EKF turns the posterior variance from two discrete values into a continuous curve and recovers the thickness ordering of the lag multiplier: 30 mm and 50 mm land within 0.1 of the fitted truth (8.74 against 8.78, 10.86 against 10.77). The 15 mm case is biased low (4.68 against 8.23) because its rising phase is too short to identify, which is the honest cost of buying information late rather than a tuning failure. The scalar tracker reports a single 0.224 at every thickness and never expresses how much it does not know."
